 that age  range  are likely to get their kids vaccinated  so it's a much lower level of  support both alberta boys have been  released from hospital and are now  recovering at home  well there have been no deaths related  to missing in canada there have been  dozens of children hospitalized across  the country and in the u.s 48 kids have  died a rare but serious risk to children  related to covet 19.  heather urex west global news calgary  covet 19 kept americans home last  thanksgiving but this year millions are  on the move airline bookings are up more  than 100 compared to 2020 but those  travel plans may hit some turbulence  that's because starting tomorrow agents  with the transportation safety  administration or tsa are required to be  vaccinated and many are refusing  jennifer johnson has more  in the midst of the busiest travel week  since the pandemic began tsa agents are  facing a monday deadline to either get  vaccinated or face the consequences  there is the potential if you  do not have an approved exemption and  you are not vaccinated that you will  lose your job an estimated 2 million  passengers a day are passing through  america's airports for the 10 days  surrounding thanksgiving but travel  experts wanted possible delays as  thousands of tsa agents are still  refusing to get the shot travelers are  building in extra time we just know that  we have to be here earlier and  anticipate that there's going to be more  lines and things as of mid-october an  estimated 40 percent of tsa agents had  not been vaccinated the administration  hasn't provided an updated number but  says it's greatly improved whether the  unvaccinated will be immediately fired  is unclear all federal employees face  the monday deadline but the biden  administration is encouraging each  agency to investigate before terminating  we have a lot of employees who've asked  for either medical or religious  exemptions as well and so we'll go  through the process of looking at each  one 