ouldn't it's been understood  from day one that i'm the first curator  here with no collection  but the flip side of that is that every  collection in the rom  is up to me to interpret in a way the  rom has always addressed climate impacts  in its exhibits how the dinosaurs became  extinct or more current issues like the  threat to the giant sperm whale  it's now dr brothers job to take the  conversation about climate change to the  next level  it's a timely issue evidence of global  warming from wildfires to floods isn't  hard to find and the cop 26 conference  on climate change just wrapped up with  newfound promises to cut carbon  emissions there's no question dr  brothers says climate change can be  scary fear is not a really productive  emotion and so i don't want to just  shock people or get people feeling  scared about what's happening with  climate change there's definitely a fine  line to walk there in terms of also not  losing the gravity of the situation of  gravity of the reality of it but with  climate change nothing good will happen  without first starting the conversation  mike drolite global news toronto  and that is global national for this  sunday night i'm jeff semple tonight's  your canada is an episode migma trail in  northern new brunswick the picturesque  147 kilometer trail is the only canadian  destination to earn a coveted spot on  national geographic's list of the most  exciting places to visit in 2022 and  it's easy to see why thanks for watching  donna friesen will be back here at the  anchor desk tomorrow have a great night  [Music]
 

